        "cliff": "a creature is one Actor type with a different configuration",
        "teaches": [
          "A creature and a person are the same Actor type. What separates them is subType, the damage order, which characteristics are shown, and whether the token is linked.",
          "behaviour.diet and behaviour.pattern are the two fields that say how it hunts and what it wants.",
          "group.count is a pack of them on one sheet: value is how many are left, max how many there were.",
          "speed.fly is a Speed Band index and not a number of metres; speed.ground and speed.swim are metres."
        ],
        "trap": "A creature needs characteristics.hits.base above 0 AND the string hits in config.damageOrder. Miss either and the four creature damage states go quiet — no error, no warning, and a creature that cannot be hurt. The Armour trait below carries its number in params[].num as well as in value, because nothing recomputes it at load: an Armour (4) with a null num is Protection 0."
      }
    }
  },
